{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "note": "Detector corpus for the Tenjin publish scan, kept as data so the tenjin server-side ingest gate can vendor it verbatim (see plans/2026-08-18-session-observer.md, PR 2a). Every entry is one detector: `id` is the stable finding `check`, `tier` is the finding severity, `match` is either a JS regex (pattern + flags) or the name of an algorithmic detector a consumer must implement, `excerpt` is the redaction policy, and `skip` names a suppression predicate. Several entries may share an `id`; they are one detector expressed as more than one pattern. Patterns adapted from gitleaks are MIT and attributed in NOTICE.md.",
